%I A398315 #16 Sep 02 2026 18:05:46
%S A398315 1,1,3,23,427,18638,2014160,560030641,411339286008
%N A398315 Number of asymmetric semicomplete digraphs with n nodes.
%C A398315 A semicomplete digraph is a digraph in which, for every pair of distinct vertices u and v, at least one of the arcs (u,v) and (v,u) is present. Asymmetric means that the automorphism group is trivial.
%H A398315 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A398315/a398315.pdf">The 23 asymmetric semicomplete digraphs on 4 vertices</a>
%F A398315 a(n) = Sum_{[H] <= S_n} mu(1,H)*3^(q(H)-r(H))/|N_{S_n}(H)|, where the sum is over conjugacy classes of subgroups H of S_n, q(H) is the number of H-orbits on ordered pairs of distinct points, r(H) is the number of H-orbits on unordered pairs, and mu is the subgroup-lattice Moebius function.
%e A398315 For n=4 there are 23 asymmetric semicomplete digraphs up to isomorphism, so a(4)=23.
%Y A398315 Cf. A047656 (labeled semicomplete digraphs), A051504 (asymmetric digraphs).
%K A398315 nonn,more,new
%O A398315 1,3
